  "responsive": {
    "desktop": {
      "name": "Desktop ≥1280px",
      "note": "One workbench. Full-width work surface capped at 1060px of content, with the conversation bar docked underneath. The target profile is a nested overlay on the workbench, never a page of its own."
    },
    "tablet": {
      "name": "Tablet 900–1280px",
      "note": "Resizable split with a 360px conversation minimum. Target tabs wrap; the brief stays collapsed."
    },
    "mobile": {
      "name": "Mobile <900px",
      "note": "Stacked. Conversation first with the live question pinned, work surface below, sticky segmented jump control, composer always reachable, brief becomes a one-line expandable header. Hit targets stay at 44px."
    }
  },
  "invariantRules": [
    "The conversation is visible on every stage, including target selection, profiles, drafts and preflight.",
    "The first question is about the goal. No client is required, and none is ever selected automatically.",
    "A campaign can have no client, one client, several clients, a coalition, or an internal sponsor.",
    "The Directory lives inside target selection. Users can also add targets by hand.",
    "Meri recommends targets but never pre-adds them.",
    "Every target row opens a profile, and profile facts are labelled verified, needs confirmation, stale, conflicting, or restricted.",
    "Target-specific context is scoped to one person and cannot appear in another target’s draft.",
    "Saved audiences are a source of targets, never a delivery mode.",
    "Personalized separate, same-message separate, and shared-thread delivery are three distinct choices.",
    "Large campaigns generate representative samples first and review exceptions first.",
    "Sending always requires the dedicated preflight confirmation. Typing “send it” opens preflight and never sends.",
    "The screen is not split. One workbench, with the conversation docked across the bottom and its history expandable over the work.",
    "Meri’s live question is always on screen next to the input, and the full transcript is one click away without leaving the stage.",
    "A typed instruction is never applied on its own. Meri proposes, the effects are named, and the user applies.",
    "The workflow is resumable. Leaving and returning restores the same checkpoint, and interrupted generation resumes without rewriting finished drafts.",
    "Sponsor, audience class and target class are separate. A coalition sponsor writing to agency staff and member companies is a supported campaign, not an exception.",
    "Nothing is written to memory after a send unless each proposal is approved individually."
  ],
